  "Question": "If \\(n\\) is an integer, which of the following numbers must divide \\((n+3)^2-n^2\\)?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "2",
    "B": "6",
    "C": "9",
    "D": "3"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\((n+3)^2-n^2=(n+3+n)(n+3-n)=3(2n+3)\\), which must be a multiple of \\(3\\). Since \\(2n+3\\) is odd and is not necessarily a multiple of \\(3\\), the expression is not necessarily divisible by \\(2\\), \\(6\\), or \\(9\\).",
